                    |CKBChapter 12 - Parties and Community
                   |BKB-----------------------------------

|YKOParties hold two to six players. Members can coordinate on a private
channel, share experience from kills, follow a leader, and optionally split
gold. Use |YKBassist <player>|YKO to join the intended fight.

Useful party commands:

  |YKBpoffer <player>|YKO              Start a party or invite someone
  |YKBpstatus|YKO                      Review members and status
  |YKBpsay <message>|YKO               Speak privately to the party
  |YKBpemote <message>|YKO             Emote privately to the party
  |YKBpfollow on|YKO / |YKBpfollow off|YKO
  |YKBpsplit <amount>|YKO              Split coins once
  |YKBpautosplit on|YKO / |YKBpautosplit off|YKO
  |YKBpleader <player>|YKO             Transfer leadership
  |YKBpname <name>|YKO                 Name the party
  |YKBpboot <player>|YKO               Remove a member
  |YKBpleave|YKO                       Leave the party

Parties are only one part of the community. Channels connect players across
the game. Clans are player-run organizations; kingdoms have rulers,
nobility, and shared projects. Patrons and deities add another path of
alignment and devotion. Darkwind's Discord keeps the conversation going
outside the game.

Be clear about the destination, loot, quests, and retreats before a dangerous
run. Keep quest spoilers off public channels, wait for disconnected members
when possible, and ask before joining another player's fight.

You have reached the end of the Newbie Tome, not the end of Darkwind.
Return to |YKBhelp guide|YKO for the current eight-stage path and ask on the
|YKBnewbie|YKO channel whenever you need a hand.|000

